ce"},{"text":", in the same order. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"per-incidence array is indexed by edge position. A view is a snapshot, so its own positions","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"never change, but they are valid for the hypergraph only until its next mutation: the view of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the mutated hypergraph numbers the incidences afresh (on ","type":"text"},{"code":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", inserting","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one cell shifts every later incidence by one).","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every index member reads the base’s rows, shifted where they hold hyperedges:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"successorIndices(ofIndex: i)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"code":"outHyperedgeIndices(ofIndex: i)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" plus n, and of "},{"code":"n + p","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" it is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"targetIndices(ofHyperedgeAt: p)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"; "},{"code":"predecessorIndices","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"code":"inHyperedgeIndices","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" plus n, or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"sourceIndices","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Graph algorithms therefore run on the view without hashing a vertex. The view"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"does not offer "},{"code":"_withSuccessorIndexRows","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", whose contract needs edge positions in row order."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Costs are as for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IncidenceGraphView"},{"type":"text","text":": O(1) reads on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IncidenceList"},{"type":"text","text":", which stores its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"incidences; on another base a hyperedge’s incidence numbers are a range, O(1), "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edges[q]"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"binary-searches and selects by rank, O(log m + ⌈n\/64⌉) on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix"},{"type":"text","text":", and a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"outEdges"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"inEdges"},{"type":"text","text":" is computed from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_memberRank"},{"type":"text","text":", O(d·⌈n\/64⌉) on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]}],"sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"A directed hypergraph’s incidence graph, read lazily from its storage: a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on ","type":"text"},{"code":"0 ..< n + m","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" whose vertex ","type":"text"},{"code":"i < n","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the hypergraph’s vertex","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"index ","type":"text"},{"code":"i","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and whose vertex ","type":"text"},{"code":"n + p","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is hyperedge ","type":"text"},{"code":"p","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", with an arc ","type":"text"},{"code":"i → n + p","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for each source","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"i","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" of ","type":"text"},{"code":"p","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"n + p → j","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for each target ","type":"text"},{"code":"j","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". A vertex on both sides of ","type":"text"},{"code":"p","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" gives the 2-cycle","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"i → n + p → i","type"